# ADHD Content Engine

When creating or revising ADHD blogs, FAQs, or pillars in `apps/siya-health`, follow **`apps/siya-health/docs/ADHD-CONTENT-ENGINE.md`** in full, plus architecture in `ADHD-KNOWLEDGE-ARCHITECTURE.md`.

## Gate

Publish only if the URL (1) becomes definitive for a topic Siya must own, OR (2) materially strengthens a pillar/cluster. Else stop and re-scope.

## Pipeline

Knowledge Gap → Brief → SEO Review → Outline → Link Map → Medical Checklist → Draft → Publish.

**Default:** deliver Brief + Outline first; wait for approval before full HTML unless the user says draft now.

## Quality bar

Do not ship encyclopedia-only pages. Prefer entity ownership (e.g. ADHD + binge eating, not “what is BED”). Include when relevant: prevalence early, comparison tables, myth boxes, practical day scenes, medication deep-dives for real search (Vyvanse/BED etc.), Siya evaluation what-to-expect, EEAT, conversion close that reframes toward ADHD eval.

## Linking SOP

Every net-new ADHD piece: 1 pillar · 2 blogs · 1 FAQ · 1 service (screening / Meet & Greet / adhd-care by funnel) · 1 local if live.

## CTA by funnel

Awareness → screening · Trust → Meet & Greet · Evaluation → /adhd-care · never Zocdoc/Spruce as cold primary.

## KW strategy

Win intersections and process/commercial investigation Siya can own. Do not fight Mayo on bare disease definitions unless Siya already owns the category.

## EEAT

Dr. Sneh Pandey MD, Internal Medicine, ABOM; last reviewed; real references; honest review status.

## Local city treatment pages

Follow `apps/siya-health/docs/LOCAL-ADHD-TREATMENT-PAGE-ENGINE.md`. Phase 5 only: state hub → city; anti-doorway; commercial investigation; Meet & Greet or `/adhd-care` CTA.
